      solution: `<p> (d)<br/> Gantry girders are designed to resist the following loads associated with the operation of an<br/> overhead crane:<br/> <strong>•Gravity loads:</strong> These are the vertical forces from the weight of the girder itself, the crane<br/> bridge, and the lifted load. This is the primary vertical load the girder must support.<br/> <strong>•Lateral loads:</strong> These are horizontal forces caused by the acceleration or braking of the crab<br/> (trolley) as it moves across the crane bridge. They act perpendicular to the length of the<br/> girder.<br/> <strong>•Longitudinal loads:</strong> These are horizontal forces caused by the acceleration or braking of the<br/>entire crane as it moves along the gantry rails. They act parallel to the length of the girder. </p>`,
